  "restrictions": [
    "Do not execute every phase blindly.",
    "Do not create public assets in this foundation phase.",
    "Do not create a new engine.",
    "Do not duplicate existing operation logic.",
    "Do not publish by default.",
    "Do not run IndexNow send without explicit approval.",
    "Do not infer missing governance decisions."
    ,"Do not certify a new or migrated calculator as FULL_STANDARD_ACCEPTED when visual status is VISUAL_VALIDATION_NOT_EXECUTED."
    ,"Do not render calculator recommendations without approved configuration and eligibility evidence."
    ,"Do not treat the canonical FGTS reference as a literal template or copy its domain content."
    ,"Do not accept a non-institutional primary theme without approved variation evidence."
    ,"Do not invent or hide the governed visible updated-at value."
    ,"Do not accept screenshot, full-page capture, viewport-dependent or raster-only reports."
    ,"Do not rewrite editorial or SEO heritage during technical calculator migration."
    ,"Do not migrate an existing calculator without the regression baseline gate."
    ,"Do not infer governed consumers from text search."
    ,"Do not certify a governed engine with a stale visible rule representation."
    ,"Do not force NO_CENTRAL_LEGAL_RULE_REQUIRED calculators into the legal update system."
    ,"Do not automatically migrate SPECIALIZED_REVIEW_REQUIRED calculators."
    ,"Do not mark MIGRATION_COMPLETED when canonical visual family, public asset integrity, rendered result, human acceptance or rollback gates are unresolved."
    ,"Do not homologate a published migration before public post-deploy validation."
    ,"Do not infer an individual calculator PASS from aggregate batch status."
    ,"Do not generate a NEW_ARTICLE or MIGRATED_ARTICLE with unresolved editorial, freshness, source, cluster or bidirectional-link gates."
    ,"Do not apply the new article standard retroactively without explicit migration scope."
    ,"Do not represent a Guide asset as an isolated Home card."
    ,"Do not create an empty nucleus Home section before the first eligible article."
    ,"Do not use separate content sources or arbitrary order by viewport."
    ,"Do not exceed six visible nucleus articles on mobile or nine on desktop."
    ,"Do not provision a nucleus from an ambiguous topic; return MANUAL_DECISION_REQUIRED."
  ],
